  "details": "Currently, your logged-in VRChat account for the game is set per-machine. Sharing your machine means logging out and logging in to a different account. Depending on how frequently this sharing happens, this is very annoying:\n\n1. Exiting the game does not log out of the current account, so forgetting to do this might give someone else access to your account.\n\n2. Strong passwords (long with mix of letters, numbers, and special characters) are good, but very annoying to perform in VR.\n\n3. Compulsory 2-factor authentication is also good, but similarly to #2, is annoying to do in VR. \n\nIt would be good to have account switching like Steam does. It's very easy to switch back and forth between accounts that have previously logged in to the machine with \"saved credentials\" (spoiler: they are not saved credentials but instead authentication tokens that check back with Steam to see if they are still valid). For this feature, players could still force logout, or they can use a different machine to revoke the token if they happen to lose control over the machine they logged into.",
